    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick checklist for wcag 2.1 compliance for a mobile app? specifically looking for the main things we need to hit for color contrast and making sure it works with screen readers. thx",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure, here is a quick checklist for WCAG 2.1 compliance focused on color contrast:\n\n1. **Contrast Ratio:**\n   - Ensure that text-to-background color contrast ratios are at least 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text (18pt or larger, or 14pt bold).\n   - Use tools like the WebAIM Color Contrast Checker to verify these ratios.\n\n2. **Color Usage:**\n   - Do not use color alone to convey important information.\n   - Provide text alternatives for any non-text content.\n\nFor ensuring your app is screen reader friendly:\n\n1. **Language and Labels:**\n   - Use proper semantic HTML elements (e.g., headings, lists, buttons).\n   - Provide clear and meaningful text labels for each interactive component.\n\n2. **ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications) Roles and Properties:**\n   - Implement ARIA roles and properties where necessary.\n   - Ensure dynamic content updates are announced by screen readers using ARIA live regions.\n\n3. **Focus Management:**\n   - Make sure that all interactive elements are navigable using keyboard controls.\n\n4. **Visual Design:**\n   - Ensure consistent and predictable navigation.\n   - Avoid moving, changing,",
      "source": "target",
